name: "Claude Code MCP for Take-Home Assignments — Candidate Delivery Companion + Recruiter Interview Copilot"
description: |

---

## REVISION NOTE (read first)

This PRP was substantially rearchitected mid-planning. The original version built a standalone,
self-service "apply with no resume via MCP" channel with its own tokens/models, deliberately kept
parallel to the existing `Assignment`/`AssignmentSubmission` take-home flow. **That channel has been
dropped entirely** at the user's explicit direction. The new design does the opposite of the original
constraint: it **merges** MCP directly into the existing take-home Assignment flow you've already
shipped, and adds a second, separate MCP server for recruiters. If you're picking this PRP up cold,
ignore any earlier draft — this version is authoritative.

## Goal

**Feature Goal**: Give the *existing* take-home Assignment flow (candidate applies normally → gets
ranked/shortlisted → recruiter invites them to a take-home via the existing "Send Assignment" button)
an MCP companion on both ends: (1) the invited candidate can connect their own Claude Code, using the
SAME `access_token` already emailed to them, to fetch the brief and submission instructions
conversationally instead of only via the web portal link; (2) the recruiter can connect their OWN
Claude Code to a separate, authenticated MCP server and ask natural-language questions about a
specific candidate's submitted report + resume — usable live, in the interview.

**Deliverable**:
- Backend: 1 new model (`RecruiterMcpApiKey`), 2 new nullable columns on the EXISTING
  `AssignmentSubmission` table (`mcp_connected_at`, `mcp_last_seen_at`), 2 new FastMCP servers mounted
  inside the existing FastAPI app (`routers/mcp_candidate.py`, `routers/mcp_recruiter.py`), 1 new router
  for recruiter key issuance/revocation (`routers/recruiter_mcp_keys.py`).
- A small addition to the existing invite email (`_send_invite_email` in `routers/assignments.py`) so it
  includes a `claude mcp add ...` command alongside the existing portal link.
- A small addition to the existing recruiter submissions view (`JobAssignments.tsx`) showing an
  "connected via Claude Code" hint per candidate.
- New frontend surface: a recruiter settings page to generate/revoke a `RecruiterMcpApiKey`.
- **Zero changes** to `tools/nideknil-submit/` — it already POSTs to
  `/api/assignments/portal/{token}/submit`, which is exactly the right endpoint once the candidate's
  MCP connection uses the real `AssignmentSubmission.access_token`.
- Branch `feature/mcp-apply-channel` (already created) holds this work.

**Success Definition**: A recruiter invites a shortlisted candidate to a take-home exactly as they do
today. The candidate, instead of (or in addition to) clicking the portal link, runs the `claude mcp add`
command from their invite email, asks Claude Code "what's the brief for this assignment / how do I
submit", gets accurate answers sourced from the real `Assignment`/`AssignmentSubmission` row, and still
submits their transcript through the existing, unmodified web-upload or `nideknil-submit` CLI path.
Separately, a recruiter connects their own Claude Code once (via a generated API key), and can ask
"summarize how this candidate collaborated with AI" or "what should I ask them in the interview" for any
submission on a job they own — answered from the real `FluencyReport` + `Application` data, never
another recruiter's candidates.

## User Persona

**Target User (candidate)**: Someone already invited to a take-home assignment (i.e. already
resume-screened, ranked, and shortlisted through the normal apply flow) who'd rather stay in their
terminal than tab over to a web page to read the brief or remember the submit command.

**Target User (recruiter)**: A recruiter who already uses the existing take-home reports, who now wants
to prep for a specific interview by asking questions in natural language instead of re-reading a report
page and a resume side by side.

**Use Case (candidate)**: Candidate gets the invite email, runs the one-line `claude mcp add` command
from it, then instead of opening the portal link just asks Claude Code: "what's the assignment brief",
"what's the deadline", "how do I submit when I'm done".

**Use Case (recruiter)**: Recruiter has an interview with a candidate in 10 minutes. They ask their own
connected Claude Code: "get the report for submission 482", then "what should I probe on based on how
they used Claude while building it".

**User Journey (candidate)**:
1. Recruiter clicks the EXISTING "Send Assignment"/invite action on a shortlisted candidate — nothing
   changes here. `AssignmentSubmission.access_token` is generated exactly as it is today
   (`routers/assignments.py:248`).
2. The invite email (`_send_invite_email`, `routers/assignments.py:85-113`) now ALSO includes:
   `claude mcp add --transport http nideknil-assignment https://nideknil.in/mcp --header "Authorization: Bearer <access_token>"`
   right next to the existing portal link — same token, two ways in.
3. Candidate runs that command; Claude Code's `initialize` handshake hits `/mcp`; the server looks up
   the token against `AssignmentSubmission.access_token` and sets `mcp_connected_at`/`mcp_last_seen_at`.
4. Candidate asks Claude Code things like "what's the brief" → `get_assignment_brief` tool (wraps the
   EXISTING `candidate_view()` logic, `routers/assignments.py:344-364`) → "how do I submit" →
   `get_submission_instructions` tool, which returns the exact `npx nideknil-submit <access_token>`
   command (no new token, no CLI changes — it already targets the right endpoint).
5. Candidate builds the assignment, then submits through the UNCHANGED web portal or CLI — the actual
   file transfer never goes through an MCP tool call (see Known Gotchas for why).
6. Recruiter, on the existing `JobAssignments.tsx` submissions list, now also sees a small
   "🟢 connected via Claude Code, active 3m ago" hint per row, before/alongside the existing status.

**User Journey (recruiter)**:
1. From account settings, recruiter generates a `RecruiterMcpApiKey` (long-lived, revocable, shown once)
   and copies `claude mcp add --transport http nideknil-recruiter https://nideknil.in/mcp/recruiter --header "Authorization: Bearer <key>"`.
2. Connects once; persists across sessions.
3. Asks "list my submissions for job 12" → `list_submissions` → "get the report for submission 482" →
   `get_candidate_report` (merges the EXISTING `FluencyReport` fields with the candidate's `Application`
   resume/profile data) → "what should I ask them in the interview" → `generate_interview_questions` or
   a free-form `ask_about_candidate`.
4. Ownership is enforced throughout — a recruiter can only ever query submissions on jobs they own.

**Pain Points Addressed**: Candidates currently have to context-switch to a browser tab to read a brief
or recall a submit command they were only ever emailed once. Recruiters currently have to manually
re-read a report page and a resume side by side to prep for each interview; this collapses that into a
conversation they can have from their own terminal, right before walking into the room.

## Why

- This is a **quality-of-life layer on top of infrastructure you've already shipped** (the July 2026
  take-home Assignment/transcript-scoring feature), not a new acquisition channel — much lower risk than
  the earlier draft, and it reuses the EXISTING `Assignment.brief` as the "what to build" context, which
  fully resolves the "what is actually being judged" gap the earlier resume-less design had.
- The recruiter-side interview copilot is a genuinely new capability with no prior art in this codebase —
  it's the most product-differentiated piece here and worth getting right.
- Explicit product decision: the earlier standalone "self-serve apply with no resume, no email" channel
  is DROPPED — MCP now only ever activates for candidates a recruiter has already invited.

## What

Two small MCP servers layered onto existing, working infrastructure — no new candidate-acquisition
surface, no new scoring logic, no new file-upload path.

### Success Criteria

- [ ] The existing "Send Assignment" recruiter action, `AssignmentSubmission.access_token` generation,
  and the existing web-upload/CLI submission paths are **completely unmodified** in behavior — only the
  invite email's *content* changes (one more line/command), nothing about the underlying flow.
- [ ] A candidate can `claude mcp add` using their invite token and successfully call
  `get_assignment_brief` / `get_submission_instructions`, each correctly scoped to THEIR OWN
  `AssignmentSubmission` row (never another candidate's).
- [ ] `mcp_connected_at`/`mcp_last_seen_at` update on real MCP activity and are visible on the recruiter's
  existing `JobAssignments.tsx` submissions list.
- [ ] A recruiter can generate/revoke a `RecruiterMcpApiKey`, connect a distinct `/mcp/recruiter`
  endpoint, and successfully call `list_submissions`, `get_candidate_report`, `ask_about_candidate`, and
  `generate_interview_questions` — each strictly scoped to jobs that recruiter owns.
- [ ] No transcript file content is ever passed as an MCP tool-call argument — file transfer stays on the
  existing HTTP upload paths, full stop (see Known Gotchas).
- [ ] `tools/nideknil-submit/` requires zero code changes.

## All Needed Context

### Context Completeness Check

_Validated against "if someone knew nothing about this codebase, would they have everything needed to
implement this successfully?" — yes: this version reuses far more existing code than the original draft,
and every reused function is cited with file:line. The one open technical risk (mcp SDK API churn) is
still flagged as a mandatory Task 0 verification step, unchanged from before._

### Documentation & References

```yaml
# ── MCP protocol & Python SDK (unchanged from prior research — still accurate/still cited here) ──────
- url: https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-11-25/basic/transports
  why: Streamable HTTP is the current remote transport (single /mcp endpoint, POST/GET/DELETE, Mcp-Session-Id header). Replaces the deprecated HTTP+SSE transport.

- url: https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/blob/main/src/mcp/server/context.py
  why: Context object shape (ctx.headers) for reading the incoming Authorization header inside a tool.
  critical: STALENESS RISK — this SDK has had multiple Context refactors (see python-sdk issue #1684). An older pinned version may instead need `from mcp.server.fastmcp.dependencies import get_http_headers`. Run `pip show mcp` and inspect the installed package before writing the auth dependency.

- url: https://github.com/rb58853/simple-mcp-server
  why: Worked example of mounting a FastMCP `streamable_http_app()` inside an existing FastAPI app.
  critical: The mounted sub-app's lifespan does NOT auto-propagate — you must call `mcp.session_manager.run()` inside the PARENT app's own `lifespan`, or every request 500s with `RuntimeError: Task group is not initialized`. Confirmed via python-sdk issues #713, #1367, #1484.

- url: https://gofastmcp.com/deployment/http
  why: `stateless_http=True` — recommended given this backend is single-process (no --workers flag) but now serves potentially many concurrent candidates+recruiters without needing cross-call session state.

- url: https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/tutorials/security/security_best_practices
  why: A session ID must never be treated as authentication — the bearer token (access_token or RecruiterMcpApiKey) is the only real auth signal on either server.

# ── Claude Code CLI (unchanged from prior research) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
- url: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/mcp
  why: Exact `claude mcp add --transport http <name> <url> --header "Authorization: Bearer <token>"` syntax; SSE is deprecated, HTTP is current.
  critical: STALENESS RISK — re-verify with `claude mcp add --help` at implementation time; flag names have changed release over release.

- url: https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/7404
  why: `claude mcp list`/`claude mcp get` can themselves trigger a live `initialize` — don't over-read a bare handshake as "the candidate is actively working."

# ── Internal: the EXISTING flow this now plugs into — READ THIS FILE IN FULL ──────────────────────────
- file: backend/routers/assignments.py
  why: This is now the CENTER of the feature, not something to avoid. Key pieces to reuse directly:
    `_by_token(db, token)` (line 333) — token→submission lookup, reuse as-is for candidate MCP auth.
    `_own_submission(db, submission_id, recruiter)` (line 58) — ownership check, reuse as-is for recruiter MCP auth (catch its HTTPException and translate to a tool-appropriate error string, since MCP tools aren't FastAPI endpoints).
    `candidate_view(token, db)` (line 344) — exact shape to return from `get_assignment_brief`.
    `_assignment_open(a)` (line 75) — reuse to tell the candidate if the assignment is still accepting submissions.
    `_send_invite_email(...)` (line 85) — MODIFY this to append the `claude mcp add` command to the email body.
  gotcha: Do NOT duplicate any of this logic in the new MCP routers — import and call the real functions. The earlier draft of this PRP avoided importing from this file on purpose (parallel-system constraint); that constraint is explicitly LIFTED now.

- file: backend/models.py
  why: `AssignmentSubmission` class — find its exact current column list before adding `mcp_connected_at`/`mcp_last_seen_at`; note it already has `application_id` (nullable FK to `applications.id`) — this is how the recruiter tools reach the candidate's resume/profile data.
  pattern: New tables need nothing beyond the ORM class (`Base.metadata.create_all` at main.py:40 auto-creates them). Altering an EXISTING table (`assignment_submissions`) needs a raw-SQL entry in the `_MIGRATIONS` list (main.py:68-279) — find an existing `DateTime`/`TIMESTAMP` column addition in that list to copy the exact SQL type used (don't guess between `TIMESTAMP` and `TIMESTAMP WITHOUT TIME ZONE` — match whatever convention is already there).

- file: backend/services/fluency/pipeline.py, transcript_parser.py, scrubber.py, store.py
  why: UNCHANGED — the existing `execute_fluency_analysis`/`dispatch_fluency_analysis` pipeline, already wired to `AssignmentSubmission`/`FluencyReport`, needs zero modification. The MCP layer never touches scoring; it only reads the results afterward (`get_candidate_report`) or points the candidate at the existing submit paths.

- file: backend/models.py — `FluencyReport` class (~line 844 area, per earlier research) and `Application` class (~line 588)
  why: `get_candidate_report`/`ask_about_candidate` need to join `AssignmentSubmission` → `FluencyReport` (existing FK) and `AssignmentSubmission.application_id` → `Application` (existing nullable FK) to merge score/dimensions/summary with resume_text/candidate profile in one response.

- file: tools/nideknil-submit/bin/cli.js
  why: Confirm (don't just assume) that its hardcoded target `${apiBase}/api/assignments/portal/${token}/submit` (line ~171) is unchanged and still correct — it should need ZERO modification in this version of the plan, since the token flowing through MCP now IS the real `AssignmentSubmission.access_token` this CLI already expects.

# ── Internal: patterns to copy for the NEW pieces (RecruiterMcpApiKey, MCP routers) ────────────────────
- file: backend/routers/auth.py
  why: `require_recruiter` dependency — reuse for the JWT-authenticated key-issuance endpoint (`POST /api/recruiter/mcp-keys`). The MCP tool calls themselves are NOT JWT-authenticated (they use the long-lived key instead) — don't conflate the two auth mechanisms.

- file: frontend/src/pages/JobAssignments.tsx
  why: Lines ~26-50 — the existing conditional `setTimeout`-recursion polling pattern for this exact submissions list. Add the `mcp_connected_at`/`mcp_last_seen_at` display here, reusing the SAME polling call (no new endpoint needed if these fields are already included in the existing submissions response — verify `schemas.SubmissionResponse` and add the fields there if missing).
```

