### Known Gotchas of our codebase & Library Quirks

```python
# CRITICAL (the central design decision of this version): NEVER pass transcript file content as an
# MCP tool-call argument. A candidate's Claude Code session would have to read the entire .jsonl file
# into ITS OWN context before it could pass it as a string argument — for multi-MB transcripts with
# ~35% base64 image content (per this codebase's own measured fluency-pipeline stats), that burns the
# candidate's token budget just to submit a file, may get truncated, and duplicates what the existing
# nideknil-submit CLI already does correctly (reads the file and POSTs raw bytes directly, never
# touching any LLM's context window). MCP in this design is ONLY for: reading the brief, checking
# status, and getting the submit command — the actual bytes always travel over the existing HTTP upload
# paths (web portal or CLI), unchanged.

# CRITICAL: mcp Python SDK API surface has churned across releases (Context location,
# streamable_http_app() naming). BEFORE writing routers/mcp_candidate.py / mcp_recruiter.py, run
# `pip show mcp` and inspect the installed package's actual mcp/server/context.py (or its absence) —
# do not assume `from mcp.server.context import Context` works without checking. This is Task 0.

# CRITICAL: mounting streamable_http_app() inside the existing FastAPI app WITHOUT wiring
# `mcp.session_manager.run()` into the parent app's own `lifespan` causes every MCP request to 500 with
# "RuntimeError: Task group is not initialized". main.py currently has no lifespan defined — you're
# ADDING one, not modifying an existing one. With TWO mcp servers, use `contextlib.AsyncExitStack` to
# enter both session managers inside that one lifespan.

# GOTCHA: this version DELIBERATELY reuses code from routers/assignments.py (_by_token, _own_submission,
# candidate_view, _assignment_open) — the earlier draft of this PRP explicitly avoided that. That
# constraint no longer applies; import and call these functions directly rather than re-implementing
# them. Do NOT, however, change their existing behavior/signatures — the take-home flow's existing
# callers (the web portal routes) must keep working exactly as they do today.

# GOTCHA: claude mcp list / claude mcp get can themselves trigger a live `initialize` against your
# server — a candidate idly checking their MCP config can look identical to a real connection. Treat
# mcp_connected_at/mcp_last_seen_at as "has touched the MCP server," not "is actively working right now."

# GOTCHA: single Uvicorn process today, no --workers flag — persist connection status to the DB
# (mcp_connected_at/mcp_last_seen_at columns), never an in-memory flag, consistent with every other
# stateful feature in this codebase.

# GOTCHA: no Alembic in this repo. The NEW RecruiterMcpApiKey table needs nothing beyond the ORM class
# (auto-created via Base.metadata.create_all at main.py:40). Only the ALTER on the EXISTING
# assignment_submissions table needs a raw-SQL entry in the _MIGRATIONS list — match the exact
# TIMESTAMP/DateTime SQL type convention already used elsewhere in that list, don't guess.

# GOTCHA: no test suite exists anywhere in this repo (zero test_*.py files). Validation below is
# manual/integration-based, matching how the rest of this codebase has actually been verified.

# GOTCHA: rate-limiting risk is now much lower than the earlier draft (tokens are recruiter-invited, not
# self-issued by anonymous strangers) — still add a light per-token/per-key call-rate guard on both MCP
# servers as a hygiene measure, but this is no longer launch-blocking the way open self-service issuance
# was.
```

## Implementation Blueprint

### Data models and structure

```python
# backend/models.py

class RecruiterMcpApiKey(Base):
    """A long-lived, revocable bearer credential a recruiter generates from their account settings
    to connect THEIR OWN Claude Code to the recruiter-only MCP server (/mcp/recruiter). Deliberately
    NOT the recruiter's JWT — JWTs are short-lived session tokens, wrong shape for a static CLI
    bearer header."""
    __tablename__ = "recruiter_mcp_api_keys"

    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True, index=True)
    recruiter_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey("users.id"), nullable=False)
    key = Column(String(64), unique=True, index=True, nullable=False)  # secrets.token_urlsafe(32)
    created_at = Column(DateTime, server_default=func.now())
    last_used_at = Column(DateTime, nullable=True)
    revoked_at = Column(DateTime, nullable=True)  # non-null => key rejected on every auth check

    recruiter = relationship("User", foreign_keys=[recruiter_id])


# On the EXISTING AssignmentSubmission class, add TWO columns:
#   mcp_connected_at = Column(DateTime, nullable=True)   # first successful MCP handshake
#   mcp_last_seen_at = Column(DateTime, nullable=True)   # bumped on every subsequent MCP tool call
# _MIGRATIONS entries in main.py (match the existing TIMESTAMP type convention exactly — verify first):
#   "ALTER TABLE assignment_submissions ADD COLUMN mcp_connected_at TIMESTAMP"
#   "ALTER TABLE assignment_submissions ADD COLUMN mcp_last_seen_at TIMESTAMP"
```

### Implementation Tasks (ordered by dependencies)

```yaml
Task 0: VERIFY mcp SDK API shape against the actually-installed/pinned version
  - RUN: pip show mcp (or deliberately pick+pin a version if not yet installed)
  - INSPECT: the installed package's mcp/server/context.py (or fastmcp/dependencies.py) to confirm
    whether `Context.headers` or `get_http_headers()` is the real API for THIS version
  - INSPECT: FastMCP's exact method for getting a mountable ASGI app (streamable_http_app() or current
    equivalent)
  - OUTPUT: record the confirmed shape before writing Task 5/7 — do not guess from research citations alone

Task 1: MODIFY backend/requirements.txt
  - ADD: pinned `mcp` package version confirmed in Task 0

Task 2: MODIFY backend/models.py
  - IMPLEMENT: RecruiterMcpApiKey class (see Data models above)
  - IMPLEMENT: AssignmentSubmission.mcp_connected_at / mcp_last_seen_at (nullable DateTime columns)
  - FOLLOW pattern: existing Column/relationship style throughout models.py

Task 3: MODIFY backend/main.py — migration entries
  - FIRST: find an existing DateTime column addition in the _MIGRATIONS list (main.py:68-279) and copy
    its exact SQL type string
  - ADD: the two ALTER TABLE assignment_submissions statements for mcp_connected_at/mcp_last_seen_at
  - VERIFY: RecruiterMcpApiKey needs no migration entry — picked up by Base.metadata.create_all (line 40)

Task 4: CREATE backend/services/mcp_bridge.py
  - IMPLEMENT: mark_mcp_connected(db, submission) -> sets mcp_connected_at if unset, always bumps
    mcp_last_seen_at, idempotent on repeated calls
  - IMPLEMENT: issue_recruiter_key(db, recruiter) -> RecruiterMcpApiKey (secrets.token_urlsafe(32))
  - IMPLEMENT: revoke_recruiter_key(db, key_id, recruiter) -> ownership-checked, sets revoked_at
  - IMPLEMENT: get_merged_candidate_context(db, submission) -> joins AssignmentSubmission -> FluencyReport
    (existing FK) and AssignmentSubmission.application_id -> Application (existing nullable FK), returns
    a single dict with report fields (score/summary/dimensions/highlights) + resume_text + candidate name
    — this is the shared context both get_candidate_report and ask_about_candidate/
    generate_interview_questions build on
  - DEPENDENCIES: models from Task 2
  - PLACEMENT: backend/services/mcp_bridge.py

Task 5: CREATE backend/routers/mcp_candidate.py
  - IMPLEMENT: `mcp = FastMCP("nideknil-assignment")` (or Task-0-confirmed equivalent)
  - IMPLEMENT: an auth helper reading `ctx.headers["authorization"]`, validating `Bearer <token>` by
    calling the EXISTING `_by_token(db, token)` from routers/assignments.py (import it — do not
    reimplement), then calling mark_mcp_connected() on every successful call
  - IMPLEMENT tool `get_assignment_brief()` -> calls the EXISTING `candidate_view()` logic
    (routers/assignments.py:344) for this submission's assignment, returns the same shape
  - IMPLEMENT tool `get_submission_instructions()` -> returns a string with the exact
    `npx nideknil-submit <access_token>` command (the SAME token, no new token minted) plus the existing
    web portal URL as an alternative
  - DEPENDENCIES: Task 4, routers/assignments.py's existing helpers (imported, not duplicated)
  - PLACEMENT: backend/routers/mcp_candidate.py

Task 6: CREATE backend/routers/recruiter_mcp_keys.py
  - IMPLEMENT: POST /api/recruiter/mcp-keys (Depends(require_recruiter)) -> issue_recruiter_key(), returns
    {key, connect_command} shown ONCE (standard API-key UX)
  - IMPLEMENT: DELETE /api/recruiter/mcp-keys/{key_id} (Depends(require_recruiter)) -> revoke_recruiter_key()
  - PLACEMENT: backend/routers/recruiter_mcp_keys.py

Task 7: CREATE backend/routers/mcp_recruiter.py
  - IMPLEMENT: a SECOND, distinct `FastMCP` instance — never share one instance/auth model with Task 5
  - IMPLEMENT: an auth helper validating against RecruiterMcpApiKey.key (revoked_at IS NULL), updating
    last_used_at on success
  - IMPLEMENT tool `list_submissions(job_id: int | None = None)` -> submissions on jobs the recruiter owns,
    optionally filtered
  - IMPLEMENT tool `get_candidate_report(submission_id: int)` -> ownership-checked by calling the EXISTING
    `_own_submission(db, submission_id, recruiter)` from routers/assignments.py (import it; catch its
    HTTPException and translate to a tool error string), then get_merged_candidate_context()
  - IMPLEMENT tool `ask_about_candidate(submission_id: int, question: str)` -> same ownership check, answers
    from get_merged_candidate_context()'s fields (report + resume), NOT the raw transcript by default —
    keeps cost/latency bounded
  - IMPLEMENT tool `generate_interview_questions(submission_id: int)` -> same ownership check, drafts 4-5
    questions from the same merged context (cheap addition given the context is already assembled)
  - CRITICAL: never let a recruiter query a submission on a job they don't own — test this explicitly
  - PLACEMENT: backend/routers/mcp_recruiter.py

Task 8: MODIFY backend/main.py — mounting & registration for BOTH MCP servers
  - ADD: a `lifespan` async context manager entering BOTH session managers via `contextlib.AsyncExitStack`
  - ADD: `app.mount("/mcp", candidate_mcp.streamable_http_app())` and
    `app.mount("/mcp/recruiter", recruiter_mcp.streamable_http_app())`
  - ADD: `app.include_router(...)` for recruiter_mcp_keys_router
  - PRESERVE: all existing router registrations, CORS config untouched

Task 9: MODIFY backend/routers/assignments.py — invite email only
  - MODIFY: `_send_invite_email()` (line 85) to append the `claude mcp add --transport http
    nideknil-assignment <mcp_url> --header "Authorization: Bearer <token>"` command to the email body,
    right after the existing portal link
  - PRESERVE: every other line of this file untouched — this is a one-line addition to an email string,
    not a behavior change to the endpoint logic

Task 10: MODIFY backend/schemas.py + routers/jobs equivalent for submissions
  - IMPLEMENT: add `mcp_connected_at: datetime | None` / `mcp_last_seen_at: datetime | None` to
    `schemas.SubmissionResponse`
  - VERIFY: `_submission_response()` (routers/assignments.py ~line 67) already uses
    `schemas.SubmissionResponse.model_validate(s)` — confirm the new columns flow through automatically
    once added to the model+schema, no extra plumbing needed

Task 11: MODIFY frontend/src/pages/JobAssignments.tsx
  - IMPLEMENT: render a small "connected via Claude Code, active <Xm> ago" hint per submission row when
    mcp_last_seen_at is present, using the data already coming back from the existing polling call (Task 10
    makes it available) — no new endpoint, no new polling loop

Task 12: CREATE frontend/src/pages/RecruiterMcpSettings.tsx
  - IMPLEMENT: generate a RecruiterMcpApiKey, display connect_command ONCE with a clear "won't be shown
    again" warning, list/revoke existing keys
  - MODIFY frontend/src/App.tsx: register the route

Task 13: ADD light rate limiting (hygiene, not launch-blocking in this version)
  - IMPLEMENT: a simple per-token/per-key call-rate guard on both MCP servers' auth helpers (Task 5 & 7),
    using last_seen_at/last_used_at + a call-counter, to prevent a runaway loop from one connection
  - PLACEMENT: services/mcp_bridge.py
```

### Implementation Patterns & Key Details

```python
# Pattern: FastAPI app lifespan wiring for BOTH mounted MCP sub-apps (backend/main.py)
import contextlib
from routers.mcp_candidate import mcp as candidate_mcp   # Task 5
from routers.mcp_recruiter import mcp as recruiter_mcp    # Task 7

@contextlib.asynccontextmanager
async def lifespan(app: FastAPI):
    async with contextlib.AsyncExitStack() as stack:
        await stack.enter_async_context(candidate_mcp.session_manager.run())
        await stack.enter_async_context(recruiter_mcp.session_manager.run())
        yield

app = FastAPI(lifespan=lifespan, title="Nideknil", ...)  # merge with existing FastAPI(...) call
app.mount("/mcp", candidate_mcp.streamable_http_app())
app.mount("/mcp/recruiter", recruiter_mcp.streamable_http_app())

# Pattern: candidate MCP auth REUSES the existing assignments.py helper directly (backend/routers/mcp_candidate.py)
from mcp.server.context import Context   # CONFIRM import path per Task 0
from routers.assignments import _by_token          # genuine reuse, not a mirror
from services.mcp_bridge import mark_mcp_connected

def _authenticate(ctx: Context, db: Session) -> models.AssignmentSubmission:
    headers = ctx.headers or {}
    auth = headers.get("authorization", "")
    if not auth.startswith("Bearer "):
        raise ValueError("Missing or invalid Authorization header")
    token = auth.removeprefix("Bearer ").strip()
    submission = _by_token(db, token)          # raises HTTPException(404) if unknown — catch/translate
    mark_mcp_connected(db, submission)
    return submission

@mcp.tool()
def get_assignment_brief(ctx: Context) -> dict:
    db = SessionLocal()
    try:
        submission = _authenticate(ctx, db)
        assignment = submission.assignment
        return {
            "title": assignment.title, "brief": assignment.brief,
            "evaluation_focus": assignment.evaluation_focus, "deadline": assignment.deadline,
            "company": assignment.job.company, "job_title": assignment.job.title,
        }
    finally:
        db.close()

@mcp.tool()
def get_submission_instructions(ctx: Context) -> str:
    db = SessionLocal()
    try:
        submission = _authenticate(ctx, db)
        return (
            f"When you're done, run:\n  npx nideknil-submit {submission.access_token}\n"
            f"or upload directly at {settings.FRONTEND_URL}/assignment/{submission.access_token}"
        )
    finally:
        db.close()

# Pattern: recruiter MCP tools REUSE the existing ownership-check helper (backend/routers/mcp_recruiter.py)
from routers.assignments import _own_submission   # genuine reuse
from fastapi import HTTPException

def _owned_submission(ctx: Context, db: Session, submission_id: int) -> models.AssignmentSubmission:
    recruiter = _authenticate_recruiter(ctx, db)   # validates RecruiterMcpApiKey, separate from above
    try:
        return _own_submission(db, submission_id, recruiter)   # raises HTTPException on 404/403
    except HTTPException as exc:
        raise ValueError(exc.detail)   # translate to a plain error for the MCP tool caller

@recruiter_mcp.tool()
def get_candidate_report(ctx: Context, submission_id: int) -> dict:
    db = SessionLocal()
    try:
        submission = _owned_submission(ctx, db, submission_id)
        return get_merged_candidate_context(db, submission)
    finally:
        db.close()
```

### Integration Points

```yaml
DATABASE:
  - new table: recruiter_mcp_api_keys (auto-created via Base.metadata.create_all — no migration entry)
  - migration: two ALTER TABLE assignment_submissions statements (mcp_connected_at, mcp_last_seen_at)
    appended to the _MIGRATIONS list in backend/main.py

CONFIG:
  - add to: backend/config.py — settings for constructing both MCP connect-command URLs
  - add to: backend/requirements.txt — pinned `mcp` package version (Task 0)

ROUTES:
  - app.mount("/mcp", candidate_mcp.streamable_http_app())
  - app.mount("/mcp/recruiter", recruiter_mcp.streamable_http_app())
  - app.include_router(recruiter_mcp_keys_router.router)  — /api/recruiter/mcp-keys

EMAIL:
  - routers/assignments.py's _send_invite_email() gains one appended line with the claude mcp add command

FRONTEND:
  - modified: JobAssignments.tsx renders the MCP-connected hint per row
  - new: RecruiterMcpSettings.tsx for key generation/revocation

EXTERNAL TOOL:
  - tools/nideknil-submit — NO CHANGES. It already targets the correct endpoint with the correct token.
```

## Validation Loop

_No pytest/test_*.py convention exists anywhere in this repo — validation here is manual/integration-based._

### Level 1: Syntax & Style

```bash
ls backend/pyproject.toml backend/setup.cfg backend/ruff.toml 2>/dev/null   # confirm lint config exists before assuming a command
python -c "import main"   # from backend/, venv activated — confirms the app still imports cleanly
```

### Level 2: Component Validation (manual)

```bash
cd backend && uvicorn main:app --reload --port 8000

# Simulate an existing recruiter invite (use the real endpoint, a real assignment/job) to get a real
# AssignmentSubmission.access_token, then:
TOKEN=<the real access_token from that invite>
claude mcp add --transport http nideknil-local http://localhost:8000/mcp --header "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
# Inside a real Claude Code session: "what's the brief for this assignment" -> get_assignment_brief
# "how do I submit" -> get_submission_instructions
# Confirm assignment_submissions.mcp_connected_at / mcp_last_seen_at are now set for THIS row only

# Recruiter side:
curl -s -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/recruiter/mcp-keys -H "Authorization: Bearer <recruiter-jwt>" | tee /tmp/key.json
KEY=$(python3 -c "import json;print(json.load(open('/tmp/key.json'))['key'])")
claude mcp add --transport http nideknil-recruiter-local http://localhost:8000/mcp/recruiter --header "Authorization: Bearer $KEY"
# "list my submissions for job <id>" -> list_submissions
# "get the report for submission <id>" -> get_candidate_report
# "what should I ask them in the interview" -> generate_interview_questions
```

### Level 3: Integration Testing

```bash
# Confirm the existing web-upload AND nideknil-submit CLI paths are completely unaffected
cd tools/nideknil-submit && node bin/cli.js <access_token> --dry-run   # exact existing usage, no flags added

# Confirm the invite email now contains the claude mcp add command (check logs/console-printed email
# fallback per services/email_service.py if SMTP isn't configured locally)

# Confirm a SECOND candidate's token cannot fetch the FIRST candidate's brief (multi-tenant isolation)
# Confirm a SECOND recruiter's key cannot get_candidate_report on the FIRST recruiter's submission
```

### Level 4: Creative & Domain-Specific Validation

```bash
# Security check: malformed/missing Authorization header rejected by every tool on BOTH servers
# Confirm Mcp-Session-Id (if assigned) is never treated as authentication on either server
# Confirm get_submission_instructions never embeds transcript bytes — only ever a command/URL string
```

## Final Validation Checklist

### Technical Validation

- [ ] Task 0's SDK-version verification note is recorded and every import matches it
- [ ] Backend starts cleanly with the new lifespan + BOTH mounted MCP apps
- [ ] `POST /api/recruiter/mcp-keys` requires a valid recruiter JWT; the returned key works exactly once shown
- [ ] A real `claude mcp add` + real Claude Code session can call both candidate tools AND, separately, all four recruiter tools

### Feature Validation

- [ ] Existing take-home invite/submission/scoring behavior is provably unchanged (Level 3 checks above)
- [ ] `mcp_connected_at`/`mcp_last_seen_at` show correctly on the recruiter's existing submissions list
- [ ] `get_candidate_report`/`ask_about_candidate`/`generate_interview_questions` work for the owning recruiter and are refused for any other recruiter
- [ ] No code path anywhere passes transcript file bytes as an MCP tool argument

### Code Quality Validation

- [ ] `_by_token`, `_own_submission`, `candidate_view` are imported and called from `routers/assignments.py`, not reimplemented
- [ ] `tools/nideknil-submit/` has zero diffs
- [ ] New models/routers follow existing naming/style conventions

### Documentation & Deployment

- [ ] The exact `claude mcp add` command strings (candidate email + recruiter key response) are re-verified against `claude mcp add --help` at implementation time
- [ ] New `mcp` dependency version is pinned, not left floating

---

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

- ❌ Don't pass transcript file content as an MCP tool-call argument — this is the single most important architectural constraint in this version of the plan.
- ❌ Don't reimplement `_by_token`/`_own_submission`/`candidate_view` in the new MCP routers — import and call them.
- ❌ Don't change the EXISTING behavior of `routers/assignments.py`'s endpoints while reusing its helpers — this feature is additive to that file, not a refactor of it.
- ❌ Don't touch `tools/nideknil-submit/` — it already works correctly against the real `AssignmentSubmission.access_token`.
- ❌ Don't share one `FastMCP` instance or auth helper between the candidate and recruiter servers — different trust models, keep them structurally separate even though they now both plug into the same underlying tables.
- ❌ Don't let `get_candidate_report`/`ask_about_candidate` silently return data for a submission the requesting recruiter doesn't own — fail loudly via the reused `_own_submission` check.
- ❌ Don't treat a bare MCP `initialize` as proof of active engagement — `claude mcp list`/`get` can trigger one on their own.
